{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.substrate_over_determination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.substrate_over_determination","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/MuOverDetermination.lean#L148-L165","doc":"**Substrate over-determination corollary**.\n\nFor two distinct target mass ratios `ratio_a ≠ ratio_b`\n(e.g. one from inverting the m_p anchor, one from the\nCODATA m_μ target), the unique q values that make\n`muRatio vol_4_1 q = ratio_*` for each are DIFFERENT.\n\nContrapositive: q_a = q_b ⇒ ratio_a = ratio_b. This is the\n*negation* of \"one q anchor matches both physical masses.\" ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.muRatio_injective_on_q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.muRatio_injective_on_q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/MuOverDetermination.lean#L125-L146","doc":"**Injectivity of `muRatio` on q > 1.**\n\nTwo distinct q values strictly greater than 1 give distinct\nmuRatio values. This is the precise structural fact behind\nthe over-determination finding: if `muRatio` were the unique\nfunction determining q from the muon ratio, then choosing q\nto match a DIFFERENT physical mass (m_p) would generically\ngive a DIFFERENT q than the muon-matching one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.muRatio_strictMono_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.muRatio_strictMono_anti","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/MuOverDetermination.lean#L99-L123","doc":"**Strict monotonicity of `muRatio` on q > 1** (for positive vol_4_1).\n\nSince `hbarQ` is strictly increasing on q > 1 and both\n`hbarQ q₁, hbarQ q₂ > 0`, `hbarQSq` is also strictly\nincreasing — therefore `muRatio = vol / hbarQSq` is strictly\nDECREASING in q.\n\nThe key categorical content: muRatio is INJECTIVE on q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQ_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQ_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/MuOverDetermination.lean#L83-L97","doc":"**Strict monotonicity of `hbarQ` on q > 1.**\n\nFor `1 < q₁ < q₂`, `hbarQ q₁ < hbarQ q₂` (ℏ_q is strictly\nincreasing in q since 1 - 1/q is increasing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQSq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQSq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/MuOverDetermination.lean#L78-L81","doc":"`ℏ_q² > 0` for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/MuOverDetermination.lean#L67-L76","doc":"`ℏ_q = 1 - 1/q` is strictly positive for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.muRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.muRatio","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/MuOverDetermination.lean#L59-L65","doc":"The muon mass-ratio function:\n`muRatio q = vol_4_1 / ℏ_q²`.\n\nFor `q ∈ (1, ∞)`, ℏ_q ∈ (0, 1), hence ℏ_q² ∈ (0, 1) and\nmuRatio is strictly decreasing in ℏ_q (i.e. strictly\nmonotonic in q in a specific direction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQSq","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/MuOverDetermination.lean#L56-L57","doc":"ℏ_q² for convenience. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.MuOverDetermination.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/MuOverDetermination.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The q-deformed Planck constant ℏ_q := 1 - 1/q. ","signatureChunk":0}]}